# ff1corneliacastle.rollnotes — beat-anchored annotations
# From the Cornelia Castle sessions (see cornelia-castle.md).
# Anchors cover the first 8-bar pass; the MIDI repeats the loop.

[1.1 - 1.4]
D — I. Home.

[2.1 - 2.4]
A — V. Dominant. Bass staircase D→C# underway.

[3.1 - 3.4]
Bm — vi. Relative minor.

[4.1 - 4.4]
F# — V/vi, aiming at Bm. The A# is the out-of-key giveaway.

[5.1 - 5.2]
G — IV. Harmonic rhythm doubles: two chords per bar now.

[5.3 - 5.4]
Gm — iv, borrowed from D minor. One voice slips a half step
(B→Bb over a shared root) and the light dims. Dm never sounds:
borrowing, not modulation.

[6.1 - 6.2]
D — I. Home again, briefly.

[6.3 - 6.4]
B7 — V7/ii, aiming at Em.

[7.1 - 7.4]
Em — ii. The target lands.

[8.1 - 8.4]
D/A → A — I6/4 → V turnaround. Arpeggio dissolves into scale
runs; texture change marks the cadence, delivering the loop home.
